From: Octessera kernel maintainers <kernel@octessera.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: mmc_spi: give a freshly inserted card time to power up

mmc_spi requests a 1 ms card-detect debounce. Pin controllers without
hardware debounce turn that into the core detect delay, so a card is
initialised 1 ms after the slot switch closes, before it has powered up,
and the one attempt fails until the card is reinserted. Wait 2 s instead.

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/mmc_spi.c b/drivers/mmc/host/mmc_spi.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/mmc_spi.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/mmc_spi.c
@@ -1266,10 +1266,11 @@ static int mmc_spi_probe(struct spi_device *spi)
 		goto fail_glue_init;
 
 	/*
-	 * Index 0 is card detect
-	 * Old boardfiles were specifying 1 ms as debounce
+	 * Index 0 is card detect. Without hardware debounce this value becomes
+	 * the core's detect delay; a freshly inserted card needs time to power
+	 * up, so wait 2 s before probing it.
 	 */
-	status = mmc_gpiod_request_cd(mmc, NULL, 0, false, 1000);
+	status = mmc_gpiod_request_cd(mmc, NULL, 0, false, 2000000);
 	if (status == -EPROBE_DEFER)
 		goto fail_gpiod_request;
 	if (!status) {
